.Dd February 28, 2017
.Dt PKG-WHICH 8
.Os
.
.Sh NAME
.Nm "pkg which"
.Nd display which package installed a specific file
.
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Oo
.Fl "gopqm"
.Oc
.Ar file
.Nm
.Oo
.Fl "-glob"
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl "-origin"
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl "-path-search"
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl "-quiet"
.Oc
.Oo
.Fl "-show-match"
.Oc
.Ar file
.
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is used for displaying the package that installed
.Ar file .
.
.Sh OPTIONS
The following options are supported by
.Nm :
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Xo
.Fl g ,
.Fl "-glob"
.Xc
Treat
.Ar file
as a glob pattern.
.It Xo
.Fl m ,
.Fl "-show-match"
.Xc
Show files that matched the glob pattern (requires
.Fl "-glob" ) .
.It Xo
.Fl o ,
.Fl "-origin"
.Xc
Show the origin of the package instead of name-version.
.It Xo
.Fl p ,
.Fl "-path-search"
.Xc
Search for the filename in
.Ev PATH .
.It Xo
.Fl q ,
.Fl "-quiet"
.Xc
Be quiet.
.El
.
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
The following environment variables affect the execution of
.Nm .
See
.Xr pkg.conf 5
for further description.
.Bl -bullet -offset 3n
.It
.Ev PKG_DBDIR
.It
.Ev PATH
.El
.
.Sh FILES
See
.Xr pkg.conf 5 .
.
